  "rationale": "No single step is a single point of failure, because the target can be reached by several independent routes. Every entry foothold is reachable, so the steps that feed these routes are reachable too: memoryDump, configSecret, dmzWeb, ssoLogin, browserStore, iotDevice and apiToken. The target crownData:exfiltrate is an OR step with these routes: (1) appServer feeds codeRepo, vaultRead and dbReplica; appServer is itself an OR of memoryDump, apiToken and ssoLogin, which are all reachable. (2) memoryDump feeds printServer, which feeds dbReplica. (3) configSecret feeds jumpHost, which feeds shareMount. Blocking appServer leaves routes 2 and 3. Blocking memoryDump leaves appServer (via apiToken or ssoLogin) and route 3. Blocking configSecret or jumpHost leaves routes 1 and 2. Blocking printServer, dbReplica, codeRepo, vaultRead or shareMount leaves other parents of crownData. No other step lies on every route."
